From u1557f895f706963e at groups.google.com  Wed Oct  2 05:39:06 2013
From: u1557f895f706963e at groups.google.com (Will L)
Date: Wed, 02 Oct 2013 05:39:06 +0000
Subject: ggplot2 and memory-efficient data structures
Message-ID: <edJAL0_ohkg.-rSKkRe5GSUJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/edJAL0_ohkg/m/-rSKkRe5GSUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As far as I know, ggplot2 can use data frames, but not matrices. This is a problem because data frames can be extremely memory inefficient, as I show here <http://will-landau.com/2013/05/01/ggplot2arrays>. It would be really nice if future releases of ggplot2 could use matrices and their dimnames attributes. Is anyone currently working on this?

